# Firebase native config — device-registration secrets for push
# notifications (see IOS_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md §5). Download from the
# Firebase Console, place them locally; never commit them. The iOS one is
# already covered by the blanket `ios/` rule below — listed explicitly too
# so it stays protected even if that rule is ever narrowed.
android/app/google-services.json
ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Android release signing keystore — never commit. Generated locally,
# used only by Android Studio's Generate Signed Bundle/APK wizard.
android/app/*.jks
android/app/*.keystore
android/keystore.properties

# The whole ios/ project (generated locally via `npx cap add ios`) stays
# untracked — unlike android/, which is committed because it carries
# intentional native config (AndroidManifest.xml intent-filters,
# strings.xml). Any equivalent iOS-side config (Info.plist keys,
# entitlements, signing) lives only on the machine that built it; redo
# IOS_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md's steps if the project needs regenerating
# elsewhere.
ios/

# Native build outputs — android/ is committed, but generated build
# artifacts under it never should be. android/ already has its own nested
# .gitignore covering build/, .gradle/, etc.; kept here too for visibility.
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/release/
*.ipa
*.apk
*.aab
